---
 doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst b/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst
index d9329ad..cf831b0 100644
--- a/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst
+++ b/doc/source/releases/relnotes_v0_34_0.rst
@@ -16,6 +16,17 @@ Anaconda users should use the ``conda`` command instead::
 Enhancements
 ============
 
+* A Reference whose value is a class defined at the top level of a module
+  of the model (:meth:`~modelx.core.model.Model.new_module`), or holds
+  one, such as a member of an :class:`~enum.Enum` defined there, is now
+  saved by :func:`~modelx.write_model` and exported by
+  :func:`~modelx.export_model`; both raised :obj:`pickle.PicklingError`
+  before. The saved model refers to the class by its module and name, so
+  a read model uses the class of the module it reads. Functions and
+  nested classes of such a module still raise :obj:`pickle.PicklingError`.
+  modelx 0.33 reads a model saved this way with a warning and sets the
+  affected References to :obj:`None`.
+
 * Tools can tell what a value is from the name of its class
   (:ref:`toolapi-kinds`). A tool first checks that
   ``type(v).__module__`` is a str that starts with ``"modelx."``,
-- 
